  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Marketing L P has $865M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Dell Marketing L P won 333 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2.6M and obligations down 56.0% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $818M to Dell Marketing L P in FY2026 to date, making the Department of Defense the dominant buyer this fiscal year. Historical obligations for Dell Marketing L P show $522M in FY21, $958M in FY22, $1.6B in FY23, $1.9B in FY24, and $2B in FY25. Dell Marketing L P's FY2026 obligations are concentrated in the Software Publishers market at $865M, with smaller activity in Sales Financing ($209K), a second Software Publishers entry ($199K), Computer and Computer Peripheral Equipment and Software Merchant Wholesalers ($170K), and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services ($29.5K). Dell Marketing L P also recorded smaller obligations with the Social Security Administration ($46.6M) and the General Services Administration ($917K).",
    "sections": [
